o this table, revoke access, bulk revoke, is the access actually gone, subscription grant status. Not for: IAM roles, policies or STS (use aws-iam), S3 bucket policies (use securing-s3-buckets), Clean Rooms permissions (use aws-cleanrooms), or writing catalog metadata, glossaries and forms, publishing listings, or retiring or deleting an asset that other teams are subscribed to and the order of operations that needs (use managing-data-catalog)\n\n\nServices: datazone\nTasks: deploy, audit\nPersona: data-engineer, developer, architect\nWorkload: data-analytics\n*","skill_name":"managing-data-asset-access"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"exporting-rds-to-s3","skill_description":"Exports Amazon RDS or Aurora database snapshots to Amazon S3 in Apache Parquet format for analytics, backup, or data migration. Handles snapshot selection or creation, IAM role setup, KMS encryption, S3 bucket preparation, export task execution, progress monitoring, and data verification. Use when exporting RDS/Aurora data to S3 for Athena, Glue, or Redshift Spectrum consumption.\n\nServices: rds, s3, iam, kms, athena, glue, redshift\nTasks: migrate, configure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: database, storage\n*","skill_name":"exporting-rds-to-s3"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify whether StartTranscriptionJob uses a passed IAM role or caller identity for S3 output"}

